{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "MIC",
  "chapter": 1,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "MIC.1.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.1.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The word of the LORD that came to Micah the Morasthite in the days of Jotham, Ahaz, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Hezekiah, kings of Judah, which he saw concerning Samaria and Jerusalem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.1.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.1.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear, all ye people; hearken, O earth, and all that therein is: and let the Lord GOD be witness against you, the Lord from his holy temple.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.1.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.1.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For behold, the LORD cometh forth from his place, and will come down, and tread upon the high places of the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.1.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.1.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the mountains shall be melted under him, and the valleys shall be cleft, as wax before the fire, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as the waters ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " poured down a steep place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.1.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.1.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the transgression of Jacob ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all this, and for the sins of the house of Israel. What ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the transgression of Jacob? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not Samaria? and what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the high places of Judah? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are they",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not Jerusalem?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.1.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.1.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore I will make Samaria as a heap of the field, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as plantings of a vineyard: and I will pour down her stones into the valley, and I will lay bare her foundations.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.1.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.1.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And all her graven images shall be beaten to pieces, and all her hires shall be burned with the fire, and all her idols will I lay desolate: for she gathered ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from the hire of a harlot, and they shall return to the hire of a harlot.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.1.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.1.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore I will wail and howl, I will go stripped and naked: I will make a wailing like the dragons, and mourning as the owls.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.1.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.1.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For her wound ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " incurable; for it is come to Judah; he is come to the gate of my people, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to Jerusalem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.1.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.1.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Declare ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not at Gath, weep ye not at all: in the house of Aphrah roll thyself in the dust.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.1.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.1.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Pass ye away, thou inhabitant of Saphir, having thy shame exposed: the inhabitant of Zaanan came not forth in the mourning of Beth-ezel; he shall receive from you his standing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.1.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.1.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the inhabitant of Maroth waited anxiously for good: but evil came down from the LORD to the gate of Jerusalem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.1.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.1.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O thou inhabitant of Lachish, bind the chariot to the swift beast: she ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the beginning of the sin to the daughter of Zion: for the transgressions of Israel were found in thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.1.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.1.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore shalt thou give presents to Moresheth-gath: the houses of Achzib ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a lie to the kings of Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.1.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.1.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet will I bring an heir to thee, O inhabitant of Mareshah: he shall come to Adullam the glory of Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MIC.1.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MIC.1.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Make thee bald, and poll thee for thy delicate children; enlarge thy baldness as the eagle; for they are gone into captivity from thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
